course: dictionary
lesson: 10834
title: Venue
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A venue is the place where an event happens. Events include concerts, matches, parties, meetings and competitions. «The venue for the school play is the hall.» The play happens in the hall, so the hall is the venue.
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. Look at the words near venue. In «a sports venue is a stadium», the word sports tells you the place is for sport. Ask yourself: where would this event happen? Then check that your meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Venue is a formal word, so you will often meet it in news reports and exam writing. «Change of venue» means the event moves to a different place. A venue is a noun, so you can have one venue or many venues.
fact: A venue is the place where an event happens.
fact: Examples of venues are a concert hall, a sports stadium, a school hall and a meeting room.
fact: «Change of venue» means the event moves to a different place.
fact: Venue is a noun: one venue, two venues.
fact: «Taylor Swift's Eras Tour... was reported to be the highest-grossing concert tour ever, taking over 2 billion US dollars.» Gross means the total before costs are taken away, and the venues are paid from that total.
exercise: «The venue for the school play is the hall.» What is a venue? | * The place where an event happens | The person who acts in the play | A type of music | The ticket that lets you in
exercise: In «a sports venue is a stadium», copy the word that tells you the venue is for sport. | * sports | a | stadium | is
exercise: «The match has a change of venue.» What does change of venue mean? | The tickets become cheaper | Everyone goes home early | The match is cancelled for ever | * The event moves to a different place
test: «The meeting's venue was changed to the library.» Where will the meeting now be held? | In the kitchen | At the sports ground | * In the library | On the bus
test: Which of these is a venue? | A ticket | * A stadium | A song | A sandwich
exam: In «Taylor Swift's Eras Tour... crews, venues and travel are paid from it», what does venues mean? | Taxes paid on concerts | Singers who perform at concerts | * Places where the concerts were held | Tickets for concerts
